::ENG2_U05_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.V.02] The root struct means build. What does reconstruct most likely mean?{
~A. destroy completely#Incorrect. The word parts do not support this meaning.
=B. build again#Correct. The prefix re means again, and construct means build.
~C. read silently#Incorrect. This meaning is unrelated to the root struct.
~D. speak loudly#Incorrect. This meaning is unrelated to the word parts.
}

::ENG2_U05_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.V.02] Which word belongs to the same word family as construct?{
~A. contrast#Incorrect. This word looks similar but is not part of the construct word family in this lesson.
~B. constant#Incorrect. This does not share the same meaning connection.
~C. consult#Incorrect. This does not belong to the construct word family.
=D. construction#Correct. Construction shares the construct base and relates to building.
}

::ENG2_U05_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.V.01] In the sentence "The feedback was constructive," what does constructive most likely mean?{
=A. helpful and building toward improvement#Correct. Constructive connects to building and improvement.
~B. confusing and harmful#Incorrect. This does not fit the context.
~C. unrelated to improvement#Incorrect. Constructive feedback helps build improvement.
~D. impossible to understand#Incorrect. This does not match the word family or context.
}

::ENG2_U05_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Sentence: "The committee will reconstruct the schedule." Which paraphrase is accurate?{
~A. The committee will ignore the schedule.#Incorrect. This changes the meaning.
~B. The committee will destroy the schedule forever.#Incorrect. Reconstruct means build again, not destroy.
=C. The committee will rebuild or reorganize the schedule.#Correct. This keeps the meaning of reconstruct in context.
~D. The committee will read the schedule aloud.#Incorrect. This is unrelated.
}

::ENG2_U05_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.V.02] Which strategy is best for determining the meaning of a word family member?{
~A. Guess from the first letter only.#Incorrect. One letter is not enough.
=B. Use the root, prefix or suffix, and sentence context together.#Correct. Combining word parts and context gives a more accurate meaning.
~C. Ignore the sentence around the word.#Incorrect. Context helps confirm meaning.
~D. Assume every related word means exactly the same thing.#Incorrect. Related words share a base meaning but differ in precise meaning.
}
